  "notes": [
    "Both annotations are model-assisted, not independent human gold labels. Cases unchanged by v6 retain their recorded provenance.",
    "The final label equals the adopted annotation record: annotations[0] on agreement, the adopted side for adopt-a/adopt-b, and ambiguous with the union of competing spans when unresolvable. Both annotation records with their evidence are preserved in every case.",
    "state.forcedSkillIds is admitted as evidence only for the skillCandidates signal (guide sections 2 and 3 read together); every other signal cites only its question's visible fields.",
    "Ambiguous and not_queried fields are reported outside evaluable denominators and are never converted to negative labels.",
    "Public origin is not proof that an example was absent from model training.",
    "This corpus is a practical laboratory sample: it is not statistically powered and supports no production-readiness or economy claim.",
    "Preparation made zero Jev/TypeSafe provider requests and selected no thresholds; the evaluation partition is locked against policy or threshold selection.",
    "v6 replaces CAL-043, EVAL-015, and EVAL-019 with authored revision 2 inputs, fresh dual annotations, and v6 adjudication; no v5 annotations are reused. The versioned risk-correction ledger is a separate overlay over this fixture base."
